          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b02bbe737e45cd55e2def879201b7291e6042331834ba7885eba62c97735b50c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_a7342c9172d2407eb7c67d69d0756503",
      "statement": "Both Citavi hook points apply their patches through assignChecked (assign, read back, compare identity): a missing target or a write that does not take effect is logged with its consequence and the feature stays disabled instead of half-working, and patch() refuses a second wrap so unpatch() peels exactly one layer.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/features/citavi/citaviImport.ts#L65-L105",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d7e53bc6c563122527294394442652097f006c2ad0dbe1f9bddca7efb6fa318e:"
